{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs-era repaired at exact head 581adb6af44a20795c839c2370c60f91a61f25a3, against review 0e44c6fa5b0d02d339af0d4fac6371952a8da7e8. Worktree clean, whitespace clean.\n\nYour first blocker was a genuine falsehood in text I wrote to fix an earlier blocker, and I confirmed it in the code before repairing rather than taking the probe on trust. fold.go roleGrantActive short-circuits: it checks the grant is directly active, then returns true immediately if the grant is a membership, and only otherwise consults membershipBasis. So presenting \"its membership basis is live\" as one of three conditions applying to every grant is false for exactly the case a reader is most likely to be holding — an ordinary ratified membership grant, which has no basis because it is the membership. The conditions are now stated per grant kind, with the genesis seed as the sole exception to ratification, and your genesis-retirement measurement is quoted as the consequence.\n\nYour second blocker was a self-contradiction: the text said retiring \"the ratification\" has the same effect as retiring the grant, twenty lines after establishing the disjunction. Retiring ratifications ends a grant only by exhausting them, and retiring one of two changes nothing. Repaired, and the typo at 53-54 with it.\n\nThe part not in your report, which I want on the record because it is the same mistake one level down. Fixing only the two cited passages would have left the corrected rule contradicted twice more in the same section: the citation-order table and the liveness paragraph both stated the membership rule universally, and both were now false in the way you had just described. Both are explicitly scoped to non-membership authority grants, with the reason given once where the two kinds are introduced. The \"two ways that happens\" transition, which had lost its antecedent, now names the two ways and who they apply to. I have made this exact error twice this session — repairing an instance and leaving the class — so I would rather you check whether the sweep is complete than take my word that it is.","body":{"commit":"581adb6af44a20795c839c2370c60f91a61f25a3","path":"docs/reference.md"}}